Plain-language summary (not a substitute for the terms above): use it,
build with it, make money with what you build — just don't repackage
and sell the tool itself, and leave a review if you use it. These terms
apply for as long as the copyright holder chooses to offer them.

Note: this is a custom license, not a standard OSI-approved one (MIT,
Apache, etc. don't support usage restrictions like #2 and #3). If you
need airtight legal terms for a specific situation, have a lawyer look
this over — but for a personal project handing out free use with a
couple of ground rules, this says what it means to say.
